attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 23, `infB` to `rsmI`, are carried by 95 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 5% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 95 to 100% of them, fewest at column 9, `yhbW`, 95% {S1}.

@variable **The first fork and variable stretch follows**, columns 24 to 42, all shell, carried by 54 to 89%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2, P}. Columns 24 to 27, `yraK` to `yraH`, are [[fimbrial proteins]] {S2, Q}. Then columns 28 to 31, `agaI` to `agaB`, are [[galactosamine transport]] {S2, Q}. The spine at columns 43 to 47, `garD` to `garK`, is [[galactarate and glycerate]] {S3, Q}.

@model **The model names about as many genes on the spine columns as on the fork and variable ones**, 95 against 94%, and hesitates less there, 0.13 against 0.31 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 25, `yraJ`, is a variable column, 0.93 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on a fork.** Columns 77 to 79, `uxaA` to `sstT`, are carried by 79 to 87% of chromosomes, all persistent {S8}. The last column is `sstT`, in 79% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 95% of genes**, 0.18 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.39 against 0.13 bits, and names fewer genes, 91% against 96% {C}.

